--TEST--
a `<T>` written between a `new` target and its `(` is refused on a user-declared class — ADR 0007 §§ 1, 3
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The grammar reads the list here exactly as it does at a call site, so this
// is a type error rather than a parse error. Type variables stay
// compiler-owned: a user-declared class never has one to bind.
class Box {}
new Box<int>();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0441]: `Box` takes no type arguments
  --> case.nvs:6:9
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
